WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.000
Recently, Jeff Bezos announced that he&nbsp;
would be going to space with his brother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.440
on July 20 using New Shepard. This would not only&nbsp;
make him the first billionaire to go to space&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:14.640
but more importantly the first owner to use his&nbsp;
own rocket. It should also be mentioned that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:20.160
this will be New Shepard’s first crewed flight to&nbsp;
space. Considering this, Jeff’s spaceflight is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:26.400
a joyride by any means. No, it’s a statement piece&nbsp;
specifically designed to destroy the skeptics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.680
For years, people have talked down on Blue Origin&nbsp;
discounting their achievements as mere copies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:36.480
and laughing at their slow pace. But, as&nbsp;
Jeff Bezos steps down from Amazon to fully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.800
focus on Blue Origin, the trajectory of&nbsp;
Blue Origin is about to radically change.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.840
So, here’s the story of Blue Origin and&nbsp;
how Jeff Bezos will ravage the haters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:53.040
Before we jump into the video, let’s address the&nbsp;
elephant in the room which is of course SpaceX.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:58.640
There’s no question that SpaceX is way ahead&nbsp;
of Blue Origin and that’s unlikely to change.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:05.200
But that’s ok. Blue Origin does not need to be the&nbsp;
best space company out there to be a leader in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:11.200
industry. This video is about how Blue Origin will&nbsp;
disprove the notion that the company is a joke&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:16.400
and how Blue Origin will grow to be the number #2&nbsp;
space company in the world. With that being said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.800
let’s take a look back at the roots of Blue&nbsp;
Origin. Blue Origin was originally founded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:27.840
on September 8, 2000 which is ironically almost 2&nbsp;
years before SpaceX. At the time, Jeff Bezos was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:33.360
actually in a pretty rough position financially&nbsp;
as that was during the midst of the dotcom crash.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:40.400
Amazon stock had already crumbled from $113&nbsp;
to just $45, but the fall was far from over.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:47.760
By September of 2001, Amazon stock would fall to&nbsp;
under $6 per share which wiped out 95% of Jeff’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:53.840
wealth. Fortunately, Amazon stock has since&nbsp;
recovered to well over $3000 per share today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.840 --> 00:02:00.080
but that rise was by no means guaranteed at the&nbsp;
time. Clearly, Jeff ended up starting Blue Origin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:05.520
during uncertain times, but something that was&nbsp;
absolutely certain though was his love for space.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.760
You see, Jeff had been dreaming of pushing forward&nbsp;
the space industry since his high school years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:14.800
In fact, Jeff wrapped up his 1982 high&nbsp;
school valedictorian speech with quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:21.280
“Space, the final frontier. Meet me there.” So,&nbsp;
Jeff would invest the money he did have into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:26.160
rocket engine development. No one really knows the&nbsp;
specifics as to what they were working on as Blue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:31.120
Origin was extremely secretive with their plans,&nbsp;
but we did get a couple of hints here and there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:37.600
In 2003 for instance, Blue Origin would start to&nbsp;
buy large portions of land in Texas presumably for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:43.360
testing purposes. And in 2004, Jeff Bezos would&nbsp;
actually have a lunch meeting with Elon Musk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:48.480
to discuss their space companies and the future&nbsp;
of the industry. According to Elon Musk, Jeff was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:54.400
constantly proposing ideas that SpaceX had already&nbsp;
tried and discarded. Apparently, he advised Jeff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:58.960
to trash these ideas, but Jeff would go ahead&nbsp;
and try them anyway to find out for himself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:05.040
Jeff wasn’t in any rush to build up the company&nbsp;
as fast as possible. By this point, amazon stock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:10.480
recovered quite a bit. So, he was in no rush&nbsp;
to win commercial contracts or launch a rocket.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:15.680
He strongly believed that slow and steady was the&nbsp;
key to victory. That’s how he built up Amazon, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:20.640
that’s how he was going to build up Blue Origin.&nbsp;
In fact, their mission statement proclaims, “We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:25.600
are not in a race...We will go about this step by&nbsp;
step because it is an illusion that skipping steps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:33.200
gets us there faster. Slow is smooth, and smooth&nbsp;
is fast.” Evidently, Jeff didn’t care about speed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:38.720
but what he did care about was experimentation&nbsp;
and innovation. One of his earliest ideas was to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:44.240
vertically land New Shepard which dates back to&nbsp;
2005. A common misconception is that vertically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:50.800
landing rockets/boosters was Elon’s idea and that&nbsp;
Jeff copied it. But in reality, this idea is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:55.680
original to either of these guys. The idea to&nbsp;
vertically land rockets is a classic within the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:02.480
space industry and dates back to the 1930s. For&nbsp;
instance, in the 1959 movie, the Sky Calls, we can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:08.720
see a rocket landing that’s basically identical to&nbsp;
that of Falcon 9 and New Shepard. So, this is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:15.680
a new idea by any means. SpaceX and Blue Origin&nbsp;
simply made this fan fiction a reality. Anyway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:21.280
moving forward, Jeff would do an interview in 2008&nbsp;
where he revealed his plans for New Shepard. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:26.880
goal was to conduct an uncrewed launch in&nbsp;
2011 and a crewed launch in 2012. Clearly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:32.240
these dates wouldn’t quite pan out, but that’s&nbsp;
basically the case with every space plan. In April&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:37.280
of 2015, Blue Origin would finally conduct their&nbsp;
first uncrewed test flight of the New Shepard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:43.200
Unfortunately, the booster would crash during the&nbsp;
landing, however, the capsule would land safely.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:48.080
Though it took forever for Blue Origin to conduct&nbsp;
their first launch, there is definitely some truth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:53.280
to Jeff’s philosophy of slow and steady wins the&nbsp;
race. Since that first launch, Blue Origin has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:59.520
conducted 14 launches of the New Shepard, all of&nbsp;
which were 100% successful. And this is why I am&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:05.440
so confident that Jeff will indeed fly to space&nbsp;
this summer. The July 20th date may not hold up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:10.560
because of logistical, technical, and/or weather&nbsp;
related delays. But these factors shouldn’t push&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:14.880
back the flight more than a couple of days&nbsp;
or weeks in the worst case. Completing this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:20.400
flight will bring Blue Origin more interest than&nbsp;
ever before. As we discussed at the beginning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:24.640
Jeff would be the first owner to ride in his&nbsp;
own rocket. And the fact that he’s willing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:29.520
be part of the first crew speaks volumes about how&nbsp;
much he trusts his product. With Virgin Galactic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:34.800
for instance, Richard Branson has been teasing a&nbsp;
ride on SpaceShipTwo for years. Richard, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:39.600
was never willing to be the first to test his&nbsp;
planes. And throughout their history, a pilot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:45.120
was even killed during a test flight. So, let’s&nbsp;
not forget that rockets and space are extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:50.800
dangerous and things have gone wrong. As a result,&nbsp;
Jeff completing a flight on new shepard would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:56.160
give potential customers a level of confidence&nbsp;
that is unparalleled within the industry. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:01.680
I know a lot of you guys will point to Falcon 9’s&nbsp;
reliability, and that is absolutely true. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:07.760
New Shepard and Falcon 9 aren’t really comparable.&nbsp;
Falcon 9 is an orbital rocket that cost $10s of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:13.440
millions per seat. New Shepard is a suborbital&nbsp;
rocket with a ticket cost of about $250,000&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:17.120
per seat. Also, I know that the first New&nbsp;
Shepard ticket was sold for $28 million,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:22.400
but that was more of a fundraising effort and&nbsp;
the buyer paid a massive premium to be the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:27.680
civilian to ride New Shepard. With that being&nbsp;
said, Blue origin will dominate the sub $1 million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:32.480
space tourism industry over the next decade which&nbsp;
will be the vast majority of the space tourism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:37.760
market itself. Blue Origin’s only competitor&nbsp;
within this market is Virgin Galactic who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:42.560
doesn’t have nearly as strong of a track record.&nbsp;
So, Jeff’s spaceflight will solidify the company’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:47.920
future in space tourism and be the first step&nbsp;
in disproving the haters. New Shepard is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:52.560
a suborbital rocket though. To solidify their&nbsp;
position as a space leader, they also need to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:57.440
have a strong orbital rocket, and that’s where&nbsp;
New Glenn comes into play. Blue Origin has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:02.400
developing new glenn since 2012 and they currently&nbsp;
plan to launch the behemoth in the fourth quarter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:09.280
of 2022. Now, that date may not come true, but&nbsp;
New Glenn development truly is in the homestretch.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:14.080
By far the hardest part of developing a rocket&nbsp;
is the rocket engines. New Glenn is supposed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:20.080
use the BE-4 engine, but New Glenn is not the only&nbsp;
rocket using this engine. United Launch Alliance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:24.800
actually contracted Blue Origin to build BE-4&nbsp;
engines for their upcoming Vulcan Centaur rocket&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:29.600
which is still expected to launch at the end of&nbsp;
this year. This means that the engines are almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:35.120
ready to go. Assuming that the Vulcan Centaur&nbsp;
launches at the end of this year or early 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:42.960
New Glenn can’t be far behind. Even if they don’t&nbsp;
hit the q4 2022 date, 2023 and 2024 would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:48.880
highly likely launch dates. Let’s just say that we&nbsp;
see New Glenn take flight by 2025. With a payload&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:54.400
capacity of 45 metric tons, New Glenn will be the&nbsp;
second largest fully reusable rocket ever built,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.400 --> 00:08:00.240
only beaten out by Starship. If New Glenn beats&nbsp;
Starship to a successful orbital flight, New Glenn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:05.440
would temporarily be the largest fully reusable&nbsp;
rocket. This of course comes along with a plethora&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:10.960
of commercial contracts and interest. Blue Origin&nbsp;
has already attracted several commercial partners,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:15.520
and I’m sure they’ll make quite a bit of money as&nbsp;
a launch provider. But, what’s really interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:20.560
with new glenn though is lunar missions. Since&nbsp;
the very beginning, returning to the moon has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:26.240
been one of Jeff Bezos primary intentions. They’ve&nbsp;
got the Blue moon and the human landing system,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:30.560
and though Blue Origin didn’t win the Artemis&nbsp;
contract, they aren’t giving up on the moon by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:35.680
any means. If we say that Blue Origin completes&nbsp;
a crewed spaceflight using New Glenn by 2030,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:39.840
it’s quite likely that Blue Origin will get&nbsp;
humans to the moon in the early to mid 2030s.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:45.200
Again this will be nearly a decade after&nbsp;
SpaceX, but that doesn’t take away from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:49.920
fact that Blue Origin could very well reach the&nbsp;
moon before any other country. This means that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:54.480
Blue Origin will be one of three organizations&nbsp;
that have the ability to put humans on the moon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.040 --> 00:09:00.320
And I’m confident that Blue Origin will be the&nbsp;
one to leverage this ability. Here’s the thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:05.680
SpaceX’s main goal is to make humans a&nbsp;
multiplanetary species by settling Mars. So, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:12.160
moon will not be their primary focus. Meanwhile,&nbsp;
Nasa’s main focus is research and development,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:16.960
so they don’t really care about the moon beyond&nbsp;
building a research base and conducting in depth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:20.960
research. This gives Blue Origin the perfect&nbsp;
opportunity to be the ones that commercialize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:25.600
the moon and near earth space throughout the&nbsp;
2030s. This includes space manufacturing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:30.240
space energy production, space tourism,&nbsp;
space hotels, and so on and so forth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:34.880
Jeff’s primary thesis has always been&nbsp;
“We have to go to space to save earth.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:38.000
Though Jeff thinks it’s important&nbsp;
to research other planets like Mars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:42.960
he thinks the primary purpose of space is to serve&nbsp;
people on Earth whether that be reducing pollution&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:48.320
on earth by manufacturing in space or providing&nbsp;
people on earth with an exotic travel destination.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:53.120
Considering this, over the long term, I&nbsp;
believe that SpaceX will be the colonists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:58.240
government space agencies will be the scientists,&nbsp;
and Blue Origin will be the commercialists. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:02.160
this role starts as soon as Jeff Bezos&nbsp;
successfully completes his spaceflight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:07.040
destroying the haters and opening up the gates&nbsp;
for commercialization. Do you guys think that Blue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:12.720
Origin is overly scoffed at? Comment that down&nbsp;
below. Also, drop a like if you would like to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:17.600
Blue Origin disprove the skeptics. And of course,&nbsp;
consider joining our discord community to suggest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:21.200
future video ideas and consider subscribing&nbsp;
to see more questions logically answered.

